## Task 2: Dynamic Gates

### [mgpu] filter — DB-05 light regression gate

Result: TIMEOUT/DEADLOCK at first test
Test: 'gpu_execution - table_gpu cache warm cross-GPU hazard (follow-up #17)'
Status: TIMED OUT after 1800s (MCP budget)
Outcome: SIGTERM at test_table_gpu_cache_warm_mgpu.cpp:208 after 1 test case (22 assertions OK, 1 fatal)

Sub-test followup investigation: ran [mgpu] excluding [followup-17]:
  Test: 'physical_hash_join - repeated BUILD_PROBE queries don't wedge on leftover state'
  Result: FAILED with 'gpu_execution error: Invalid Error: SiriusExecuteQuery error: Invalid Error: Resource deadlock avoided'
  Source: glibc std::shared_mutex recursive-lock detection (POSIX EDEADLK).

Sub-test 2: 'physical_order - small sort rangecheck regression':
  Result: FAILED with same 'Resource deadlock avoided' error

[mgpu] passed: 0/16 (target 16/16). FAIL
[mgpu] exit=non-zero, runtime>1800s. FAIL
[mgpu] assertions: <100 (target ≥ 79091). FAIL

ROOT CAUSE: P1 RAII lock-scope self-deadlock — exactly as warned by 18-03 SUMMARY.
  - 18-02 wires gpu_pipeline_task::compute_task to hold std::vector<mutable_data_batch> processing_handles
    for the lifetime of op->execute() (R5 lock-and-hold).
  - Each mutable_data_batch holds std::unique_lock<std::shared_mutex> on the batch.
  - Operator code in execute() (migrated by plans 18-03/18-04) takes scoped to_read_only/to_mutable
    accessors on the SAME batches — same-thread re-lock on a non-recursive shared_mutex → glibc
    detects EDEADLK and aborts.
  - 18-03 SUMMARY documented this as a runtime audit deferral; runtime now confirms it.

